# ARC-LABS is a byte-fidelity product: the whole value proposition is that a
# vault this app touches is byte-identical to what Obsidian wrote. Git's
# autocrlf would silently rewrite line endings on checkout and destroy the
# compatibility fixtures — .canvas files are LF, real notes are CRLF, and both
# must survive a clone unchanged.
#
# So: git does no line-ending translation anywhere in this repo. Ever.
* -text

# Fixtures are oracles. Treat them as binary so nothing can normalise them.
fixtures/** -text -diff
